(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:actor/wave 3), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-laundry-machine-operation :finalize-washing-operation :finalize-drying-operation :finalize-pressing-operation :authorize-washer-run :authorize-dryer-run :authorize-press-run :proceed-with-washing-run :proceed-with-drying-run :proceed-with-pressing-run :finalize-plant-safety-clearance :declare-machine-safe-for-operation :declare-laundry-batch-safe-for-shipment :clear-batch-for-shipment :override-plant-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799008152-cloud-itonami-isco-8152-weaving-knitting-machine-operators-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the washing run" "proceed with the drying run" "proceed with the pressing run" "authorize the washer run" "authorize the dryer run" "authorize the press run" "finalize the washing decision" "finalize the washing operation" "finalize the drying operation" "finalize the pressing operation" "finalize the laundry-machine operation" "finalize the laundry machine operation" "declare the machine safe for operation" "declare the washer safe for operation" "declare the dryer safe for operation" "declare the press safe for operation" "declare the laundry batch safe for shipment" "declare the batch safe for shipment" "clear the batch for shipment" "clear the laundry batch for shipment" "finalize the plant safety clearance" "declare the plant safety cleared" "override the plant safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override plant safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799008157), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-work-record :flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/laundry-plant-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-launderer :no-plant :no-actuation :unknown-op :scope-excluded-action)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "8157"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799008157: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8157 Laundry Machine Operators plant scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8157\n-- Laundry Machine Operators** only. This is Wave3 (production/trades);\nWave0/1/2 are 100% complete, and Wave3 batches 1-13 (78 occupations)\nalready landed before this one.\n\n`gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8157` returned a clean\n404 before any work began -- this was a genuinely fresh scaffold, not a\nresume of prior partial work.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8157\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8157\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Laundry Machine Operators\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`. This ADR and\nits companion registry edit promote the `8157` entry to `:implemented`.\n\n**Industrial-laundry equipment hazard dimension.** Laundry Machine\nOperators run industrial washers, dryers and pressing equipment -- a\nreal heat/steam-burn hazard, an entanglement hazard from rotating\ndrums and pressing mechanisms, and detergent/chemical exposure. This\nactor does NOT model direct laundry-machine operation authority or\nplant-safety-clearance authority. It is deliberately restricted to\nPLANT SCHEDULING and LOGISTICS COORDINATION around the occupation\n(production-run/inventory/progress-record logging, crew/shift\nscheduling, safety-concern escalation, and detergent/linen-stock\nprocurement coordination) -- never the machine-operation-execution\ndecision or the plant-safety-clearance decision itself, and never an\noverride of a plant safety officer's judgment. The closed proposal-op\nallowlist structurally excludes any op that could directly finalize\nsuch a decision, and the governor independently, permanently\nhard-blocks any proposal whose rationale text names such a\nfinalization action, regardless of the declared `:op` or confidence --\nthis is not an escalation path a human can approve through, it is an\noutright, structural refusal at every maturity level.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8152`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8152)\n(Weaving and Knitting Machine Operators -- a closely related\nindustrial-textile-machine safety pattern, independently re-cloned and\nread in full this session). Its `millcoord.{store,advisor,governor,\nactor}` module split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph shape, closed\nop-allowlist and scope-exclusion self-trip-guard design translate\nalmost 1:1 onto this occupation's own hazardous-machinery scheduling/\nlogistics coordination scope, so this ADR's `laundrycoord.*` modules\nfollow the same shape with domain terms substituted (weaver ->\nlaunderer, mill -> plant, mill safety officer -> plant safety officer,\nweaving/knitting-operation-execution -> machine-operation-execution,\nmill-safety-clearance -> plant-safety-clearance).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8157` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for laundry machine\noperators, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Laundry Plant\nScheduling Coordination Advisor ⊣ LaundryCoordGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different\nlibrary coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **plant scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never laundry-machine operation authority** -- it must NEVER be\ndesigned to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\nmachine-operation-execution decision or a plant-safety-clearance\ndecision, nor override a plant safety officer's judgment.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- production-run/inventory/progress data\n  logging only\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n  only\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a heat/steam-burn hazard/\n  entanglement-hazard/detergent-chemical-exposure/equipment-condition\n  concern, ALWAYS escalates immediately, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- detergent/linen-stock procurement\n  proposal only\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles a machine-operation-execution finalization decision or a\nplant-safety-clearance finalization decision -- these are structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely, not merely gated behind\nescalation.\n\n### Five HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Launderer unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered launderer (crew member) record\n   (`:no-launderer`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the\n   launderer is.\n2. **Plant unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered laundry plant/line record (`:no-plant`).\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`; the governor never dispatches hardware\n   itself and never operates laundry-machine equipment itself).\n4. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`).\n5. **Scope-excluded action** -- the proposal's `:op` or `:rationale`\n   must never name a machine-operation-execution finalization, a\n   plant-safety-clearance finalization, or a plant-safety-officer-\n   judgment override (`:scope-excluded-action`), REGARDLESS of the\n   declared `:op` or confidence. This is a hard, PERMANENT block --\n   there is no maturity level or confidence at which this actor may\n   auto-commit or human-approve its way past this rule; it is an\n   outright refusal, not an escalation.\n\n### Escalation gates (always human sign-off)\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's always-escalate path). The only channel by\n  which the robot may surface a heat/steam-burn/entanglement/\n  detergent-chemical-exposure/equipment-condition observation -- it\n  never resolves the concern itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000) -- always needs human sign-off,\n  independent of confidence (boundary verified as exclusive by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`: exactly-at-threshold\n  commits, over-threshold escalates).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, CLAUDE.md)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare NOUNS (e.g.\n\"detergent\", \"steam\", \"drum\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- and this vertical's domain\nvocabulary is an especially sharp case of that risk, because routine\nwork-log/task text legitimately names washer/dryer/press components\nand consumables by name (e.g. a task literally described as \"routine\nwasher drum, dryer heat and press steam maintenance task with\ndetergent/linen-stock check\" -- equipment/consumable identification,\nnot a proposal to finalize a laundry-machine run or clear a machine as\nsafe). `laundrycoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization ACTION PHRASES (\"proceed with the washing\nrun\", \"finalize the laundry-machine operation\", \"declare the plant\nsafety cleared\", \"override the plant safety officer's judgment\"),\nnever bare nouns, and is checked only against the proposal's\n`:rationale` field (the advisor's own generated text), never against\nraw `:task` input text.\n`laundrycoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-\ntrip-on-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test driving the\ndefault mock-advisor across all four allowed ops with a task field\ncontaining exactly those bare equipment/consumable nouns, asserting\nnone of them ever hard-trip the finalization-scope rule. Green on\nfirst run.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8157\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8157` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8157`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit,\n  not assumed, to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  6-agent batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 37 tests, 79 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/\n  counts` and independently re-verified against a brand-new fresh\n  clone of the pushed repository (not just the local working copy). No\n  mojibake in the Japanese violation-detail strings (0\n  replacement-byte instances grepped in the fresh clone).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-laundry-run`/`:approve-plant-\n  safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an always-escalate\n  path: rejected outright per the task's explicit guidance -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  laundry-machine operation or a plant-safety clearance exists in the\n  code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision\n  whose failure mode is a steam/heat burn, entanglement injury or\n  chemical exposure, the capability itself must not exist in this\n  actor at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"detergent\" \"steam\"\n  \"drum\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above -- this domain's own vocabulary necessarily\n  discusses washer/dryer/press components and consumables by name to\n  do its logging/scheduling job, so a bare-noun list would self-block\n  the actor's own legitimate proposals whenever a task description\n  mentions detergent, steam or a drum.\n- Naming the crew-member field `:operator-id` (matching the ISCO title\n  \"...Machine Operators\" literally): rejected -- `docs/operator-\n  guide.md` and this fleet's convention already use \"operator\" to\n  mean the deploying business/entity running the actor, so reusing the\n  same word for the individual crew member would create a confusing\n  collision (mirroring the reference's `:weaver-id` vs. \"operator\"\n  precedent); `:launderer-id` keeps the two senses distinct.\n\n## Test verification\n\nFresh clone re-run immediately before writing this ADR:\n\n```text\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\n\nTesting laundrycoord.actor-test\n\nTesting laundrycoord.governor-test\n\nRan 37 tests containing 79 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n```\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:test/counts "{:total 37, :assertions 79, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Laundry Plant Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :launderer-verification :plant-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :machine-operation-plant-safety-clearance-finalization-forbidden :plant-safety-officer-override-forbidden)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8157"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8157"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8157)), (:test/simulator :laundrycoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8157 — Laundry Machine Operators Plant Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8157)))
